hadiths[35]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7844","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told me Al-Misri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Zuhar, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Imran, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah Al-Jamali, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him He said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he sent him to Yemen: O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: “Finish your religion, and your work will suffice for you.” “This is a small hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7844 - Incorrect"
"7845","Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us, Bamru, Abdul-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Abdullah bin Saeed told us Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Two blessings that are unjustified.” Many people: health and free time “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7845 - This in Al-Bukhari"
"7846","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mawjih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah bin Abi Hind informed, about... His father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man while he was advising him: “Take advantage of five before Five: your youth before your old age, your health before your illness, your wealth before your poverty, your free time before your work, and your life before Your death “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7846 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7847","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah told me, Saeed ibn Sulaiman Al-Wasiti Sa’dawiya told me, Zakaria ibn Manzur told me. Ibn Tha'labah Ibn Abi Malik, Abu Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Sa'd, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a Then he saw a sheep with one leg strayed and said: “Do you think this sheep is easy for its owner?” They said: Yes. He said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, this world is easier for God than this for its owner, even if the world were equal to God.” “The wing of a mosquito does not give an unbeliever a drink of water from it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7847 - Zakaria bin Manzur is weak"
"7848","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Bishr bin Musa told us, Khalid bin Khadash bin Ajlan Al-Muhallabi told us, Abd told us Allah bin Wahb, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him He said: I entered upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was feverish, so I put my hand on top of the velvet and felt the heat of his fever and said: How intense your fever is, O Messenger of God. He said: “We are like that, community of prophets. The pain will be doubled for us so that the reward will be doubled for us.” He said: So I said: O Messenger of God, that is. People are more afflicted? He said: “The Prophets.” I said: Then who? He said: “Then are the righteous. If a man is afflicted with poverty until he finds nothing but a cloak, he covers it and wears it, and if one of them He will be plagued with lice until the lice kills him, and that is more beloved to them than giving to you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7848 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7849","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari told us, saying: Uthman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Yahya bin Saleh told us. Al-Wahazi, Abu Ismail Al-Sakouni told us, he said: I heard Malik bin Adi saying: I heard Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may God be pleased with them both, saying, and he On the pulpit: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, nothing remains of the world except the likes of flies passing through its atmosphere. By God “God bless your brothers among the people of the graves, for your deeds will be presented to them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7849 - It contains two unknowns"
"7850","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Suwayd bin Saeed told me, Baqiya bin Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Buhair bin Saad, on the authority of Khaled bin Maadan, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The heart of the son of Adam is like a bird, turning over seven times a day.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7850 - There is an interruption"
"7851","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Abu Aqeel told us Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Yazid bin Sinan, on the authority of Bukair bin Fayrouz, saying: He heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: “Whoever is afraid will go in, and whoever goes in will have reached the final destination. Indeed, God’s goodness is precious. Indeed, God’s goodness is precious.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7851 - True"
"7852","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Adni told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Tufail bin Ubayy bin Ka’b, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fears He entered and whoever entered has reached the final destination. Indeed, God’s commodity is precious. Verily, God’s commodity is Paradise, the trembling one has come, followed by the equivalent one, it has come. “Death and all that is in it”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7852 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7853","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bukayr, Al-Adl, told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab Al-Sha’arani told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Amr bin Abi Amr told us, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever loves his world will be harmed by his hereafter, and whoever loves his hereafter will be harmed by his worldly life, so choose what “It endures as it perishes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7853 - There is a break"
"7854","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq bin Ka’b. Ibn Ujrah, on the authority of Zainab bint Kaab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him. A man said: O Messenger of God, have you seen these diseases that It afflicts us, what do we do with it? He said: “Atonements.” Ubayy bin Ka’b said: O Messenger of God, even if it is small? He said: “A thorn, and what is above it?” He said: “Then my father prayed for himself that the illness would not leave him until he died after not distracting him from Hajj, Umrah, or jihad in the path of God. “There is no prescribed prayer in congregation.” He said: “No man touched his skin after that except that he felt its heat until he died.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7854 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7855","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed me, Abdan informed me, Abdullah informed me, Rishdin informed me, about... Amr bin Al-Harith, Yazid bin Abi Habib told me that Abu Al-Khair told him that he heard Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of him, he narrates on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “There is not a day’s work that is not completed. When a believer falls ill, the angels say: Oh. Our Lord, Your servant is so-and-so whom You have imprisoned. Then the Almighty Lord says: Conclude for him according to his deeds, until he recovers or dies. This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7855 - Rushdin Wah"
"7856","Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Abdullah bin Najiya told us, Ubayd Allah bin Omar Al-Qawariri told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith, Abd al-Wahid ibn Zayd told us, Aslam al-Kufi told me, on the authority of Murrat al-Tayyib, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: We were with Abu Bakr. Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, called for a drink and it was brought water and honey. When he brought it to his mouth, he cried and cried until his companions cried, but they remained silent, but he did not remain silent. Then he came back and cried until they thought they would not be able to ask him. He said: Then he wiped his eyes and they said: O successor of the Messenger of God, may God bless him. What made you cry? He said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw him defending something from himself, but I did not see anyone with him, so I said: O Messenger of God, what are you defending? About yourself? He said: “This world appeared to me, so I said to it, ‘Away with me,’ then she came back and said, ‘If I escape from me, no one will escape from me after you.’” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7856 - Abd Al-Samad, left by Al-Bukhari and others"
"7857","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Muhammad bin Jahdam told us, Ismail bin Jafar, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, on the authority of Qatada bin Al-Numan, may God be pleased with him He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If God loves a servant, he protects him in this world just as one of you protects his sick person with water.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7857 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7858","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Thabit bin Yazid told us, Hilal bin Khabbab told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, entered upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was on the Mat affected his side and he said: O Messenger of God, if you had a better bed than this, he said: “What do I have to do with this world? What does this world have to do with me?” By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, my likeness and the likeness of this world are nothing but like a rider who rode on a summer day and stayed in the shade under a tree for an hour of the day, then departed. “And he left it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it. “And this is witnessed by the hadith of Abdullah bin Masoud.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7858 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7859","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab bin Habib told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Al-Masoudi informed us, on the authority of Amr bin Once, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have nothing to do with this world. I am only like myself.” The example of this world is that of a rider who sat under a tree on a summer day and left it."
"7860","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz and Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Bandar Al-Zahid told us, saying: Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Al-Hasan informed us Al-Asqalani, Ibrahim bin Amr Al-Saskiki told us, Abi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rawad told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever seeks what is with God, the sky will be his shade and the earth his bed. He will not care about anything.” The matter of the world, he does not plant crops while eating bread, and he does not plant trees and eat fruits out of trust in God Almighty and seeking To please Him, so God has guaranteed the seven heavens and the seven earths His provision. They labor over it and bring it lawful, and He completes His provision without anything else. An account with God Almighty until certainty comes to him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration for the Syrians, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7860 - Rather, it is objectionable or fabricated"
"7861","Abdullah bin Ja`far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abu al-Mughirah told us, Safwan told us Ibn Amr, on the authority of Shurayh Ibn Ubaid, that Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari, when death approached him, said: O community of Ash’aris, let the witness be informed. Among you who is absent is that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The bitterness of this world is the bitterness of the hereafter.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7861 - True"
"7862","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Al-Khorasani, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Give glad tidings to this nation of prosperity, exaltation, victory, and empowerment on earth, and whoever among them does the work of the Hereafter for this world will not have it in it.” The Hereafter is a share.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7862 - True"
"7863","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Bishr bin Matar told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far al-Warkani told me, Adi bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {So whomever God wishes to guide, He will open his chest to Islam} [Al-An’am: 125] So the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “When light enters the chest, it is revealed.” It was said: O Messenger of God, does this have any knowledge that can be known? He said: “Yes, avoiding the abode of deception, turning to the abode of eternity, and preparing for death before it descends.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7863 - Adi bin Al-Fadl has fallen"
"7864","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim, Al-Adl told me, my father told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah told me, on the authority of Al-Awwam bin Juwayriyah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Four things are not afflicted except with astonishment: silence.” It is the beginning of worship, humility, remembrance of God Almighty, and the lack of something.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 Fahd bin Awf, Omar bin Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Raqaba bin Masqala, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, he said: I ate meat A lot and a lot of porridge. Then I came and sat next to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I burped. He said: “Short your belches, for most people are full.” In this world, the hungriest are the ones in the hereafter.” True."
"7865","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amrwayh Al-Bazzaz told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa told us Al-Ashayb, Uqba bin Abdullah Al-Asam told us, Abdullah bin Buraidah told us, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “When a man says to a hypocrite, ‘O my master, he has angered his Lord, Blessed and Most High.’ This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7865 - Uqba bin Al-Asam is weak"
"7866","Ahmad ibn Abi Uthman al-Zahid told me, Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib told me, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith told me, My father, Harith bin Al-Sa’ib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hamran bin Aban, on the authority of Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The son of Adam has no right to anything except these qualities: a house to cover him, a garment to cover his private parts, and a sack of bread and water.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7866 - True"
"7867","Ja`far bin Muhammad al-Khalidi told us, Abu al-Abbas told us, on the authority of Masruq, Shurayh bin Yunus told us, Sa`id bin Muhammad al-Warraq told us, Salih bin Hassan, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “O Aisha, if... You want to join me, so let this world be enough for you like a rider’s provisions. Do not make a garment until you patch it, and beware of sitting with the rich.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"7868","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Aqbi told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Ishaq bin Nasih told us, Shayban told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i bin Harash, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdullah Al-Muharbi, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Tariq, prepare for death.” “Before the descent of death” is true.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7868 - True"
"7869","Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave income to the rich, for it is possible that you do not despise The blessings of God Almighty. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7869 - True"
"7870","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Ja’far bin Abi Othman Al-Tayalisi told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Wahb told us, Saad bin Tariq reported on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The blessings of the worldly abode are for those who provide From it to his hereafter until his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, is satisfied. And wretched is the abode for he who turns him away from his hereafter and falls short of his Lord’s satisfaction, and when The servant said, “God is disgraceful to the world.” The world said, “God is disgraceful to those who disobey their Lord.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7870 - Rather, it is objectionable"
"7871","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid al-Hafiz told us, in Hamadan, Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein told us, Abu al-Yaman told us, Ufair ibn Ma`dan told us, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a servant becomes ill, God inspires His angels: O my angels, I have bound My servant with one of My fetters. If I seize him, I will forgive him, and if I pardon him, then he will sit and not commit any sin. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7871 - Afeer bin Ma’dan is weak"
"7872","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever dies doing something, God will resurrect him for it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. The condition of a Muslim and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7872 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7873","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja`far al-Aadmi al-Qari, in Baghdad, narrated to us, Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Nasih narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nasih narrated to us. Amr Al-Qurashi, Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, advised a man He said: “Avoid the world and God Almighty will love you, and abstain from what is in the hands of people and the people will love you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7873 - Khalid bin Amr Al-Qurashi is lost"
"7874","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim, Al-Adl told me, my father told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Ma’iz Al-Amiri, on the authority of Sufyan bin Abdullah Al-Thaqafi, may God be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger God spoke to me about something that I should adhere to. He said: “Say, ‘My Lord is God, then be upright.’” He said: I said: O Messenger of God, how much do I fear for myself? He said: So he took his breath and then said: “This” is “a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7874 - True"
"7875","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Ishaq bin Abdul-Wahid al-Qurashi told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Silah bin Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “A look is one of Satan’s poisoned arrows. Whoever abandons it out of fear of God, the Almighty and Majestic, will reward him with faith that will find its sweetness in his heart.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"7876","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakr bin Sahl Al-Damiati told us, Shuaib bin Yahya told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If you have four, it will not matter what you missed. “This world: keeping trustworthiness, truthfulness in speech, good character, and chaste food.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7876 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7877","Abu Hafs bin Omar bin Muhammad bin Ahmed Al-Jumahi told us, in Mecca in the house of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Masry told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Darraj, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a man did work in a rock that has no door or opening, his work would go out to the people in some form.” “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7877 - True"
"7878","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Indeed, Allah tries each one of you with balāʾ (tribulations) while He is well aware of him. ˹He tries him˺ just like one of you ˹purifies˺ his gold with fire. 
7879""","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad Al-Daqqaq bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi told us, Al-Hakim bin Nafi told us, Ufayr bin Ma’dan narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God Let one of you be tested by calamity even though he knows it, just as one of you tests his gold in fire. Among them are some, and it comes out as fine gold. This is the one whom God Almighty has saved from evil deeds, and among them are those who come out as gold, other than that. This is the one who has some doubt, and among them are those who “It will come out like black gold. This is the one who was tempted.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not bring it out.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7878 - True"
